// Adversarial stress: DebtCollector protocol 5-system pipeline under chaos — Scatter layout.
//
// DebtCollector's 5-system pipeline: track_bump_timing (early/late classification),
// accumulate_debt (add to damage debt on late bumps), build_debt (add to debt on
// early bumps via separate path), cash_out (Perfect Bump converts debt to damage),
// and cleanup_node (reset debt at node end). This stress scenario targets:
//
//   1. cashed_this_frame pierce-guard race: cash_out fires on PerfectBumped but
//      must not fire twice in the same frame if two systems independently observe
//      the same PerfectBumped message. Scatter layout + chaos input produces
//      irregular bump timing, occasionally triggering a Perfect Bump at the exact
//      frame debt is also accumulating. If the pierce-guard flag is checked before
//      the message is consumed, cash_out fires twice and debt is double-applied.
//      BoltSpeedAccurate catches any speed corruption from double damage application;
//      NoNaN catches NaN from a debt value accumulated to overflow.
//
//   2. cleanup_node cross-node isolation: when a node ends and a new one begins
//      (allow_early_end: false causes restarts), the debt accumulator must be
//      reset to exactly zero. If cleanup_node fires on a frame where accumulate_debt
//      also fires (both reading the same frame's bump events), the reset races the
//      accumulation and the next node begins with residual debt. RunStatsMonotonic
//      is not listed but NoNaN catches a NaN debt value carried across nodes.
//
//   3. Early/late classification boundary: track_bump_timing classifies bumps as
//      early or late relative to a timing window. Chaos input drives bumps at all
//      frame offsets — the boundary between early and late must be crisp. If the
//      boundary is an open vs. closed interval mismatch, a bump exactly at the
//      boundary is classified as both, triggering both accumulate_debt and
//      build_debt, doubling the debt unexpectedly. NoNaN catches the downstream
//      effect; NoEntityLeaks catches duplicate message entities from double-firing.
//
//   4. Entity lifecycle under rapid consecutive bumps: Scatter layout produces
//      varied gap widths and irregular bounce angles, driving sequences of 3-5
//      consecutive bumps with very short inter-bump intervals. Each bump produces
//      a BumpDealt message; if debt messages are not consumed before the next bump
//      fires, they accumulate. NoEntityLeaks catches unconsumed message entities.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false ensures multiple node restart cycles.
// 16 runs explore diverse Scatter cell arrangements and bump timing distributions.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 2903,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "DebtCollector")),
    ],
)
